{
  "about": "What the chat's screen record (typescript/src/cli/ui/screen.ts, python/webagents/cli/ui/screen.py) makes of what is written to the terminal. Each case starts a record of `columns` x `rows`, applies `steps` (write: text; anchor: the 1-based row a cursor position report gave; scrolled: rows the input box scrolled the terminal while the record was paused; resize: [columns, rows]), then each check asks for the `above` rows directly over the cursor: `plain` is their text (null: not all of them are known), `rendered` the text and escapes that draw them again. `reference` cases were also checked against an independent terminal emulator.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "lines, oldest first",
      "columns": 20,
      "rows": 10,
      "steps": [
        {
          "write": "one\ntwo\nthree\n"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "above": 3,
          "plain": [
            "one",
            "two",
            "three"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "reference": true
    },
    {
      "name": "rows never seen are unknown",
      "columns": 20,
      "rows": 10,
      "steps": [
